{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A stranger and a sojourner.</b> Because I am a stranger, I have no burial plot here, as it says: וּמִי לְךָ פֹה כִּי חָצַבְתָּ לְךָ פֹה קָבֶר (Isaiah 22:16). And the reason I seek to purchase it is that I am a sojourner with you — for I came to settle permanently, not merely to sojourn." "<b>Give me a burial possession.</b> They agreed that I should have a burial possession, as it says: <b>to Abraham for a burial possession from the children of Heth</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The verse citation follows the Hebrew text תוֹשָׁב rendered 'sojourner' in both occurrences; Sforno distinguishes גֵּר (stranger, i.e. one without property) from תוֹשָׁב (one who has come to settle)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:13.523573535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}